{
  "summary": "Nick Xenophon Team senator Skye Kakoschke-Moore announced her resignation from the Australian Senate after discovering she holds dual British citizenship by descent through her mother, who was born in Singapore when it was a British colony. Kakoschke-Moore had previously believed she was not a British citizen based on advice her father received from the British embassy decades earlier. She expressed being heartbroken by the revelation and said she would request the matter be referred to the high court to determine how her vacancy should be filled. She indicated her intention to continue running for the NXT and hoped to return to the Senate. Party leader Nick Xenophon described the loss as devastating but suggested it was not the end of her political career. The party also noted preliminary legal advice suggesting the vacancy may not be straightforwardly filled by a recount, citing the recent Hollie Hughes high court decision as creating uncertain legal territory."
}
```

